WEBVTT

00:02.910 --> 00:05.510
We're fortunate to have clear skies

00:04.980 --> 00:07.860
<b>Katagiri High School Sports Day</b>

00:05.510 --> 00:08.670
and perfect weather for sports day.

00:09.100 --> 00:14.350
Please practice good sportsmanship 
and enjoy this day to the fullest.

00:14.860 --> 00:18.050
Thank you, sir.

00:18.870 --> 00:21.100
And now, the pledge of fair play.

00:28.880 --> 00:30.880
<b>Gloom</b>

00:28.880 --> 00:34.380
We, the students of Katagiri High School,

00:34.380 --> 00:37.420
The class president's looking a little blue.

00:34.970 --> 00:38.680
{bg}will now demonstrate the results 
of all our training.

00:37.420 --> 00:39.320
Despite his red hair.

00:39.320 --> 00:41.390
It's quite a contrast.

00:41.390 --> 00:44.390
<i>The president actually came to school.</i>

00:45.640 --> 00:48.400
Good thing it's so cool today, huh?

00:48.840 --> 00:50.510
Lots of people are in long sleeves.

00:51.190 --> 00:52.900
Oh, you're right.

00:53.630 --> 00:58.010
Sengoku was saying, "Miyamura-kun's 
actually going to try?! That traitor!"

00:58.010 --> 00:58.780
Huh?

01:02.450 --> 01:05.860
I never had a reason to try hard before.

01:06.230 --> 01:08.610
Honestly, the whole thing bored me.

01:09.420 --> 01:13.990
But this year, I've got to beat you.

01:14.420 --> 01:17.930
And now, Katagiri High School sports day...

01:17.930 --> 01:19.120
has officially begun!

01:18.180 --> 01:21.970
<b>Sports Day</b>

02:52.020 --> 02:56.030
<b>Katagiri High School Sports Day</b>

02:52.850 --> 02:56.030
<i>With that, the east and west teams
are looking evenly matched!</i>

02:56.030 --> 02:59.780
<i>I'll bet the second-year girls'
hurdle race had everyone sweating!</i>

03:00.230 --> 03:01.940
Wouldn't you agree, Nakamine-sensei?

03:01.940 --> 03:03.290
It was incredible.

03:03.290 --> 03:04.330
There you have it!

03:04.330 --> 03:06.540
Well done, second-years!

03:06.540 --> 03:15.670
<b>West</b>

03:06.540 --> 03:15.670
<b>Miyamura • Ishikawa • Kawano • Ayasaki • Yanagi</b>

03:07.090 --> 03:10.290
Do the third-years run the hurdles next?

03:10.290 --> 03:11.170
Yep.

03:11.550 --> 03:12.780
Let's go, Sakura.

03:13.740 --> 03:15.590
Just make sure not to get hurt, Remi.

03:15.590 --> 03:17.090
Sure!

03:18.670 --> 03:22.030
Sengoku-san, let's do 
the three-legged race together!

03:18.670 --> 03:27.930
<b>East</b>

03:18.670 --> 03:27.930
<b>Hori • Sengoku • Iura • Yoshikawa</b>

03:22.030 --> 03:24.360
I don't have a partner yet.

03:24.360 --> 03:27.930
Sengoku, do topple-the-pole. 
They need another boy.

03:27.930 --> 03:29.900
I'd rather be a shellfish...

03:29.900 --> 03:32.570
<i>Next up is the third-year 
girls' hurdle race.</i>

03:34.410 --> 03:36.060
Well, I'll see you later!

03:36.060 --> 03:37.940
Good luck, Hori!

03:41.700 --> 03:49.330
<b>Flying high to the east sky!</b>

03:42.400 --> 03:44.800
I guess we're in the same race.

03:44.800 --> 03:47.380
I bet you're really fast.

03:47.380 --> 03:49.320
No, not really.

03:49.320 --> 03:52.640
<i>Yeah, right. Like I believe that.</i>

03:49.750 --> 03:54.080
<b>I shall mow down any who stand in my way.</b>

03:51.370 --> 03:54.080
I shall mow down any who stand in my way.

03:54.080 --> 03:55.620
Good luck!

03:55.620 --> 03:56.590
You can do it!

03:56.590 --> 03:57.920
Do it!

03:56.590 --> 03:58.340
Do it, west team!

03:58.340 --> 04:02.320
Hori-san, Miyamura-kun is cheering for me!

04:02.670 --> 04:05.670
I think he's cheering for
all of Team West, Ayasaki-san.

04:05.670 --> 04:07.100
Next heat, line up.

04:09.610 --> 04:12.390
I'll work hard to impress Miyamura-kun.

04:12.390 --> 04:14.870
I really don't think he 
meant you in particular...

04:13.400 --> 04:14.870
On your marks!

04:14.870 --> 04:18.110
If I win, then Miyamura-kun belongs to me,

04:18.110 --> 04:19.360
Kyon-Kyon.

04:19.890 --> 04:21.070
Kyon... Huh?!

04:21.070 --> 04:22.310
Ready...

04:23.860 --> 04:24.740
Hey!

04:25.240 --> 04:26.770
Ayasaki's fast!

04:26.770 --> 04:27.850
Is she the dark horse?

04:27.850 --> 04:30.240
<i>West's Ayasaki-san is leading heat 5!</i>

04:33.230 --> 04:37.450
<i>Uh-oh, that's gonna hurt! 
And it'll cost her time!</i>

04:34.960 --> 04:36.700
That sounded painful.

04:36.700 --> 04:38.230
I think she kicked it on purpose.

04:38.230 --> 04:39.630
Whoa...

04:42.140 --> 04:44.480
<i>Ayasaki-san had to go mess with my head.</i>

04:44.480 --> 04:45.630
<i>Damn it!</i>

04:45.630 --> 04:48.240
<i>Team East seems to be trailing behind!</i>

04:48.590 --> 04:50.180
<i>I know that, damn it!</i>

04:50.930 --> 04:54.050
That last girl on the east team 
is looking really intense.

04:54.050 --> 04:56.500
Yeah, she's in our class.

04:55.520 --> 04:57.020
<b>Her boyfriend</b>

04:57.770 --> 05:00.770
<i>East takes first! And west takes second!</i>

05:01.850 --> 05:04.900
<i>And after I told Miyamura not to slack...</i>

05:05.870 --> 05:08.140
<i>I suck.</i>

05:16.980 --> 05:18.860
Hori-san, don't give up!

05:27.430 --> 05:30.380
You're not supposed 
to cheer for the other team!

05:30.380 --> 05:32.930
Finish strong, Team East!

05:32.930 --> 05:34.650
Damn, she's fast!

05:34.650 --> 05:36.940
<i>East has suddenly picked up speed!</i>

05:40.000 --> 05:41.110
Kyon-Kyon!

05:42.320 --> 05:44.320
Enough with the "Kyon-Kyon" stuff.

05:44.570 --> 05:47.960
You and Miyamura-kun are so in love,

05:47.960 --> 05:51.140
I couldn't bear to steal him from you.

05:51.140 --> 05:52.330
<i>This little...</i>

05:53.450 --> 05:56.890
Just kidding! I've already got Sengoku-kun.

05:56.890 --> 05:59.890
It's so cute that you get flustered so easily.

05:59.890 --> 06:01.780
H-Hey!

06:01.780 --> 06:03.710
H-Hori-san, there you are.

06:03.710 --> 06:12.470
<b>Katagiri High School ~ Sports Day</b>

06:04.410 --> 06:06.130
Sorry, were you discussing something?

06:06.130 --> 06:08.610
We're done, so I'll be on my way.

06:08.610 --> 06:10.630
I'll even take this for you.

06:10.630 --> 06:12.470
Ah, thanks.

06:12.860 --> 06:14.550
How's your leg?

06:15.050 --> 06:16.530
That was quite a hurdle race.

06:16.530 --> 06:18.060
I came in last.

06:18.060 --> 06:21.000
You looked so good in practice.

06:21.000 --> 06:23.210
How come you stalled out?

06:24.110 --> 06:26.110
Because of you!

06:26.110 --> 06:31.870
<b>Scoreboard</b>

06:26.110 --> 06:31.870
<b>East</b>

06:26.110 --> 06:31.870
<b>West</b>

06:26.560 --> 06:28.990
S-So why'd you speed up at the end?

06:28.990 --> 06:30.660
That was because of you, too!

06:31.870 --> 06:33.050
<i>That's not fair!</i>

06:33.050 --> 06:35.100
The next heat is starting, 
so I'm going back.

06:35.100 --> 06:36.660
You should, too.

06:36.660 --> 06:38.090
O-Okay.

06:38.090 --> 06:39.250
And one more thing!

06:39.970 --> 06:42.010
Thanks for cheering for me.

06:43.540 --> 06:44.780
It made me happy.

06:46.370 --> 06:47.370
Sure...

06:51.920 --> 06:53.760
Check it out, Miyamura.

06:56.010 --> 06:58.600
Sawada-san's on our team.

06:58.600 --> 07:01.370
Can she even pull the tug-of-war rope?

07:02.770 --> 07:05.400
<b>Swish
\h\h\h\hSwish</b>

07:02.770 --> 07:05.400
Hori-senpai!

07:02.770 --> 07:05.400
<b>Hori going back
to her team's tent</b>

07:05.400 --> 07:07.380
Watch me compete!

07:07.380 --> 07:09.350
Sawada-san's on the other team, right?

07:09.350 --> 07:10.310
I think so.

07:10.650 --> 07:12.060
You can do it, Sawada!

07:12.060 --> 07:13.710
Go for it, Sawada-san!

07:14.410 --> 07:14.660
<b>Snub</b>

07:14.660 --> 07:15.660
What the?

07:15.660 --> 07:18.660
<b>Glance</b>

07:18.910 --> 07:19.620
<b>Grin</b>

07:22.810 --> 07:25.840
I thought maybe I was cheering too loud.

07:25.840 --> 07:28.550
Everyone loves having 
someone root for them.

07:29.420 --> 07:31.180
Even you, right?

07:31.910 --> 07:37.680
I don't think I've ever really cheered for
anyone or vice versa at sports day before.

07:37.680 --> 07:41.610
At least cheer more for your team
than our opponents, okay?

07:41.610 --> 07:44.140
It was just the heat of the moment...

07:44.140 --> 07:45.190
Sorry.

07:45.490 --> 07:49.820
Make sure you cheer for me
 on the obstacle course.

07:50.510 --> 07:53.750
Drown out the other team, will ya?

07:54.070 --> 07:56.580
<b>West, Fighting Fierce!</b>

07:54.490 --> 07:55.270
Right.

07:56.580 --> 07:58.330
<b>Disappointed</b>

07:58.860 --> 08:01.840
Hori-senpai, we lost.

08:01.840 --> 08:06.590
D-Don't let it get you down. We had
a lot of athletes on the east team side.

08:06.590 --> 08:10.750
I wanted you to see me win!

08:10.750 --> 08:12.760
This is the east team area, you know.

08:16.170 --> 08:17.870
Ishikawa-kun's up next!

08:17.870 --> 08:19.110
Let's give a great cheer.

08:19.110 --> 08:20.760
R-Right.

08:22.600 --> 08:24.950
Iura, you'd better win!

08:22.770 --> 08:26.900
<b>INTENSE</b>

08:24.950 --> 08:26.910
Get first! You hear? First!

08:26.900 --> 08:32.030
<b>Peaceful</b>

08:26.910 --> 08:29.030
Good luck, boys!

08:29.030 --> 08:32.030
Ishikawa— Y-You can do it!

08:32.030 --> 08:41.040
<b>West
<b>Pleasant</b></b>

08:32.030 --> 08:41.040
<b>East
<b>THUNDEROUS</b></b>

08:32.420 --> 08:34.850
I wish I were on Team West.

08:34.850 --> 08:36.800
If I lose, my team might kill me.

08:36.800 --> 08:37.730
Where's Sengoku?

08:37.730 --> 08:41.040
He said he's only doing
the events that everyone has to.

08:41.440 --> 08:42.540
On your marks!

08:44.980 --> 08:46.040
Ready...

08:47.150 --> 08:50.090
<i>The boys' obstacle course is underway!</i>

08:50.090 --> 08:51.920
<i>First up is the balance beam!</i>

08:51.920 --> 08:54.970
<i>East and west are neck and neck! 
Neither is giving up the lead!</i>

08:54.970 --> 08:55.600
I—

08:55.600 --> 08:57.420
Ishikawa-kun, keep it up!

08:57.740 --> 08:58.410
Ishi—

08:58.410 --> 09:01.350
Ishikawa-kun, what are you doing?!

09:01.970 --> 09:03.730
All together...

09:03.730 --> 09:06.230
Go for it, Ishikawa-kun!

09:06.230 --> 09:08.730
Again! Ready, and...

09:08.730 --> 09:11.860
Go, Ishikawa!

09:11.860 --> 09:14.860
Must be nice to have
the girls cheering for you.

09:12.400 --> 09:14.860
{bg}Go, Ishikawa-kun!

09:14.860 --> 09:18.370
Except there's one
high-pitched guy in there, too.

09:19.690 --> 09:20.870
<i>So you're finally...</i>

09:22.020 --> 09:23.580
<i>able to speak up.</i>

09:24.620 --> 09:27.300
<i>Which team will prevail?!</i>

09:27.300 --> 09:29.500
You can do it!

09:30.460 --> 09:32.090
So you tied?

09:32.090 --> 09:37.960
"Well, that must mean that Iura really
went for it," or so Yoshikawa-san said.

09:37.960 --> 09:39.430
You have my praise as well.

09:38.340 --> 09:40.600
<b>Sparkle</b>

09:39.430 --> 09:40.600
Thanks.

09:41.090 --> 09:42.690
Where are the girls?

09:42.690 --> 09:46.100
Getting ready for the cheer 
competition coming up next.

09:46.390 --> 09:49.980
<i>Now for the event the boys have been 
waiting for, the cheer competition!</i>

09:49.980 --> 09:52.480
<i>First up are the east third-year girls!</i>

09:53.780 --> 09:55.490
Come on, everyone!

09:55.830 --> 09:56.740
Say!

09:56.740 --> 09:57.490
E!

09:57.490 --> 09:58.240
A!

09:58.240 --> 09:59.010
S!

09:59.010 --> 09:59.740
T!

09:59.740 --> 10:02.740
The great-east team!

10:02.740 --> 10:04.890
I just love Senpai!

10:02.740 --> 10:10.750
<b>Disappointed</b>

10:04.890 --> 10:06.520
She's the best!

10:06.520 --> 10:08.370
I've never seen a cheer like this!

10:08.370 --> 10:10.750
Neither have I.

10:11.070 --> 10:14.760
How does her boyfriend feel about it?

10:14.760 --> 10:16.820
Yeah, he's glazed over.

10:16.820 --> 10:18.130
Figured as much.

10:18.130 --> 10:20.040
Fear not, Team West!

10:20.370 --> 10:22.140
Ready? Okay!

10:22.140 --> 10:23.640
Okay!

10:23.640 --> 10:25.140
Go, go, west!

10:25.140 --> 10:26.640
Win, win, west!

10:26.640 --> 10:28.420
We've got this!

10:28.420 --> 10:30.650
Let's go, Team West!

10:31.780 --> 10:35.740
East won over the girls, 
and west won over the guys.

10:35.740 --> 10:37.640
Do you think Remi was a little too cute?

10:37.640 --> 10:39.400
Are you listening, Sengoku-san?

10:39.400 --> 10:42.410
<i>Right, right, left, and up!</i>

10:42.410 --> 10:44.410
<i>Now punch up and to the left!</i>

10:44.410 --> 10:47.660
The strong-west team!

10:50.860 --> 10:52.140
<i>I did it!</i>

10:55.550 --> 10:57.610
Good work on the third-year cheer!

10:57.610 --> 10:59.310
Man, that was hot!

10:59.310 --> 11:00.350
Good work!

11:00.350 --> 11:01.870
Hori-san, you did great!

11:01.870 --> 11:02.800
Thanks!

11:02.800 --> 11:03.960
Yoshikawa-san.

11:04.430 --> 11:06.590
Nice job, Kono-san!

11:06.590 --> 11:08.900
The west team looked great!

11:08.900 --> 11:10.700
Y-You mean it?

11:11.260 --> 11:12.440
Thank you.

11:13.270 --> 11:15.500
For helping me practice.

11:15.920 --> 11:18.690
I didn't get to properly thank you.

11:18.690 --> 11:21.200
I-It's a bit late now, but...

11:22.070 --> 11:24.070
You're so serious, Kono-san.

11:24.070 --> 11:25.830
Not really...

11:26.720 --> 11:30.680
<i>Maybe Ishikawa-kun noticed me a little.</i>

11:31.330 --> 11:33.080
<b>West</b>

11:33.080 --> 11:35.090
<b>Sadness...</b>

11:35.400 --> 11:37.870
You knew what was coming.

11:37.870 --> 11:41.600
I just really wanted to see her 
in a cheerleading outfit.

11:40.840 --> 11:42.840
<b>Disappointment</b>

11:43.150 --> 11:45.600
Miyamura-kun, can I borrow you for a minute?

11:45.600 --> 11:52.600
<b>West, fighting fierce!</b>

11:47.180 --> 11:49.080
Do you need me for something?

11:49.080 --> 11:52.600
Yes, one of the boys is out with a cold.

11:52.600 --> 11:54.730
Could you please take his place?

11:55.220 --> 11:58.890
You aren't in any individual events, right?

11:58.890 --> 12:01.110
No, but...

12:01.730 --> 12:04.260
A-Are you sure you want me?

12:05.910 --> 12:07.990
I'm asking you, so of course!

12:10.320 --> 12:12.040
Oh, of course.

12:12.040 --> 12:13.490
I'll be right there.

12:13.490 --> 12:14.620
Thanks!

12:14.620 --> 12:16.000
You'll do great.

12:19.950 --> 12:21.740
<i>{fb}Miyamura came in third.</i>

12:21.740 --> 12:23.510
<i>{fb}What a loser.</i>

12:24.370 --> 12:28.800
<i>{fb+int}Someone more athletic should 
have entered all the events.</i>

12:30.570 --> 12:31.770
<i>{fb}It made me happy.</i>

12:31.770 --> 12:33.320
<i>You'll do great.</i>

12:33.640 --> 12:36.770
<i>Everyone loves having 
someone root for them.</i>

12:37.690 --> 12:44.940
<i>Sports day is actually kind of...</i>

12:44.940 --> 12:46.030
<b>Flying high to the east sky!</b>

12:46.030 --> 12:51.140
Next is the scavenger hunt, 
our only coed event!

12:51.140 --> 12:55.350
<i>Open an envelope, find what's written 
inside, and bring it to the finish line!</i>

12:53.360 --> 12:55.350
Glasses! Anyone wearing glasses?!

12:55.350 --> 12:56.790
Any girls with ponytails?!

12:56.790 --> 12:59.360
I'll be the first to the finish line!

12:59.360 --> 13:03.800
That's great. I can help you get
to the finish line in life, too.

13:03.800 --> 13:04.690
Hmm?

13:03.800 --> 13:05.300
<b>Someone suspicious</b>

13:05.300 --> 13:09.020
Say, Yoshikawa,
what were you supposed to find?

13:09.720 --> 13:11.730
Th-The youngest teacher.

13:11.730 --> 13:12.810
Oh?

13:12.810 --> 13:14.400
<i>East has reached the finish line!</i>

13:14.400 --> 13:16.470
<i>Yuki finished first.</i>

13:16.790 --> 13:18.320
<i>I need to get going!</i>

13:19.840 --> 13:21.570
<i>I'll finish first, too!</i>

13:24.070 --> 13:25.180
Sorry!

13:25.180 --> 13:26.730
I'll get a different one!

13:26.730 --> 13:28.040
No, you can have it!

13:28.040 --> 13:29.700
Huh? Hori-san?

13:30.950 --> 13:31.960
Miyamura?!

13:31.960 --> 13:33.340
What are you doing here?!

13:33.340 --> 13:36.580
Well, someone was absent, 
so I got asked to fill in.

13:36.580 --> 13:38.580
Hori, hurry up!

13:38.580 --> 13:40.570
Crap, I'm falling behind!

13:41.940 --> 13:42.940
Ah...

13:43.590 --> 13:46.220
<b>Flustered</b>

13:46.220 --> 13:49.500
Jeez, what is Miyamura-kun doing?

13:49.500 --> 13:52.270
Both he and Hori-san seem surprised.

13:52.270 --> 13:53.830
Book it, Miyamura!

13:53.830 --> 13:55.730
Keep it up, Kyo-chan...

13:57.950 --> 14:00.230
What're you doing over here, Sengoku?

14:00.230 --> 14:02.130
It was a close call.

14:00.230 --> 14:05.740
<b>East team</b>

14:02.130 --> 14:05.740
They were looking for a sub 
and would have entered me,

14:05.740 --> 14:06.790
but I slipped away!

14:06.790 --> 14:08.610
Y-You seem invigorated.

14:09.990 --> 14:12.540
Hey... Wait! What is this?!

14:12.540 --> 14:16.250
<i>C-Could it be that east and 
west drew the same thing?!</i>

14:16.250 --> 14:17.370
How does that happen?!

14:17.370 --> 14:19.990
I need him, Miyamura!

14:19.990 --> 14:21.500
I do, too!

14:21.500 --> 14:23.370
Hold on! You're gonna pop out my shoulders!

14:23.370 --> 14:24.750
H-Hang in there!

14:24.750 --> 14:26.430
Hang in there, Sengoku-kun.

14:26.430 --> 14:28.380
You don't need to cheer for me!

14:28.380 --> 14:31.390
No!

14:31.390 --> 14:34.390
The final two participants 
have crossed the finish line...

14:34.390 --> 14:36.060
at the same time!

14:37.040 --> 14:39.520
<i>The both seem to have brought 
the student council president.</i>

14:39.520 --> 14:41.720
Why'd you have to pick me?

14:42.290 --> 14:47.030
What did you have on your slips?

14:47.030 --> 14:49.030
<b>A skinny boy</b>

14:47.030 --> 14:49.030
<b>Student council president</b>

14:51.650 --> 14:53.000
I understand Kyo-chan.

14:53.000 --> 14:55.870
But you, Miyamura-kun!
There are plenty of other skinny guys!

14:55.870 --> 14:59.020
I thought I should find the skinniest one...

14:59.020 --> 15:01.790
You traitor!

15:01.790 --> 15:06.300
<b>Scoreboard</b>

15:01.790 --> 15:06.300
<b>East</b>

15:01.790 --> 15:06.300
<b>West</b>

15:02.730 --> 15:06.300
<i>The third-year boys' mock cavalry 
battle is starting soon!</i>

15:06.300 --> 15:10.050
<b>Announcer</b>

15:06.800 --> 15:10.050
<i>All competitors, please get ready.</i>

15:10.050 --> 15:12.050
You'll be the rider, obviously.

15:12.050 --> 15:14.050
You'll be the rider, obviously.

15:16.060 --> 15:18.750
Is it my weight again?
Why is it always about that?!

15:18.750 --> 15:20.930
You'd snap in half 
if you were on the bottom.

15:20.930 --> 15:23.330
We're not branches.

15:23.330 --> 15:26.000
If we're doing this,
Sengoku-san, let's win it!

15:26.000 --> 15:26.820
Sure.

15:26.820 --> 15:28.320
<b>Visibly
different
temperatures</b>

15:28.320 --> 15:29.250
Yay, yay!

15:29.250 --> 15:30.200
Yay, yay.

15:30.200 --> 15:31.050
Yay, yay!

15:31.050 --> 15:31.950
Yay, yay.

15:31.950 --> 15:33.940
Gimme a "Yeah!", Sengoku-san.

15:33.940 --> 15:36.340
Okay, we're going for Sengoku first.

15:34.820 --> 15:36.330
{bg}Yeah!

15:36.330 --> 15:37.370
Got it.

15:36.750 --> 15:37.830
{bg}Yeah!

15:39.580 --> 15:41.790
Yanagi-kun's on top, too.

15:40.090 --> 15:41.450
{bg}Hey, looking good!

15:41.450 --> 15:42.630
{bg}Thanks!

15:41.790 --> 15:44.830
<i>All the riders are the least 
competitive people here.</i>

15:44.830 --> 15:47.090
Upsy-daisy!

15:51.840 --> 15:54.220
I'm actually starting to enjoy this.

15:54.220 --> 15:55.030
Really?!

15:55.030 --> 15:55.720
Finally?

15:55.720 --> 15:58.590
The view from up here is great.

15:58.590 --> 16:02.230
Sengoku-san is fancying 
himself a general of sorts!

16:02.550 --> 16:05.340
Sengoku looks like he's raring to go.

16:05.730 --> 16:07.610
Time to get to it, guys!

16:07.610 --> 16:08.480
Right.

16:08.480 --> 16:11.680
Sengoku! You'd better score a point!

16:11.680 --> 16:12.860
Go, go!

16:12.860 --> 16:15.160
Hori's cheering for Sengoku.

16:15.160 --> 16:17.870
Of course. She's on his team.

16:17.870 --> 16:20.370
But doesn't that tick you off?

16:21.870 --> 16:23.800
So, what's our strategy?

16:24.200 --> 16:26.500
Sengoku's a clever one.

16:27.730 --> 16:29.580
Then how about this?

16:32.510 --> 16:36.640
Are we supposed to cheer for the rider?

16:36.640 --> 16:42.020
They're all working hard, but the guy 
on top has the most important role.

16:36.640 --> 16:45.270
<b>Detail-oriented</b>

16:42.020 --> 16:44.900
I see. The mock cavalry battle 
is pretty complex.

16:45.580 --> 16:47.270
Miyamura-kun!

16:47.270 --> 16:49.240
Good luck, Miyamura-kun!

16:49.240 --> 16:50.530
Do your best!

16:50.910 --> 16:53.520
<i>Why are they only calling Miyamura's name?</i>

16:53.520 --> 16:56.920
Sengoku-san, Ayasaki-san 
is cheering for Miyamura!

16:56.920 --> 16:58.030
Doesn't that tick you off?!

16:58.030 --> 17:00.710
We're on different teams, 
so of course she is.

17:00.710 --> 17:02.790
What are you getting at, Iura-kun?

17:02.790 --> 17:03.860
I'm sorry.

17:02.790 --> 17:04.290
<b>Visibly
different
temperatures</b>

17:04.710 --> 17:07.290
<i>Okay, teams, to your starting positions!</i>

17:07.290 --> 17:10.840
<i>Who will stand in the winner's circle?!</i>

17:11.300 --> 17:12.750
<i>Ready...</i>

17:13.880 --> 17:15.980
Get on both sides of him!

17:14.470 --> 17:15.980
Go around back!

17:21.310 --> 17:22.230
There!

17:22.230 --> 17:23.390
Maybe over here?

17:23.720 --> 17:27.310
This Team West guy is
grabbing at random! Holy crap!

17:27.310 --> 17:29.940
Hey, Yanagi, open your eyes!

17:29.940 --> 17:32.640
It won't help. I forgot my glasses.

17:31.620 --> 17:34.320
Yanagi's doing better than I thought.

17:36.790 --> 17:37.890
President...

17:39.380 --> 17:42.580
I'm taking you down!

17:46.960 --> 17:49.700
The west team can dodge like the wind.

17:49.700 --> 17:52.460
I'm pretty sure anyone could've dodged that.

17:52.460 --> 17:54.590
Miyamura, get ready to strike back!

17:54.590 --> 17:55.720
R-Right!

17:59.710 --> 18:02.050
Why's Sengoku so fired up all of a sudden?

18:02.050 --> 18:04.530
He seems to have awoken his inner general.

18:04.530 --> 18:06.850
Huh. That makes no sense.

18:07.850 --> 18:10.800
Look alive, Sengoku!

18:10.800 --> 18:12.110
Yeah, yeah!

18:12.110 --> 18:13.650
Grab him by the head!

18:13.650 --> 18:15.240
<b>Stare</b>

18:13.650 --> 18:15.240
Do you want Miyamura dead?!

18:16.290 --> 18:19.070
<i>The president is good at evading.</i>

18:19.550 --> 18:20.490
Miyamura.

18:20.870 --> 18:22.400
Can you take it in one fell swoop?

18:22.400 --> 18:24.240
I'm just about at my limit.

18:24.590 --> 18:25.830
Ishikawa-kun...

18:25.830 --> 18:29.000
<i>I see. It's a lot more tiring 
to play the horses.</i>

18:29.000 --> 18:30.450
What's wrong, Ishikawa?

18:30.450 --> 18:32.460
The top of my nose really itches.

18:32.460 --> 18:34.250
Really? Mine, too.

18:34.960 --> 18:37.120
<i>This is becoming a war of attrition.</i>

18:38.210 --> 18:39.270
<i>Okay...</i>

18:45.090 --> 18:46.600
Wh-What?

18:50.130 --> 18:51.310
President.

18:52.450 --> 18:53.870
Who is that girl...

18:56.060 --> 18:59.040
that's been sitting...

19:02.070 --> 19:03.410
on your shoulder?

19:11.770 --> 19:12.670
<i>The...</i>

19:13.140 --> 19:17.670
<i>The west team has prevailed over east!</i>

19:18.300 --> 19:22.220
Sengoku totally just
turned his back, didn't he?

19:22.530 --> 19:23.680
Yeah.

19:24.220 --> 19:26.290
Nice job, Miyamura!

19:26.290 --> 19:27.060
Aw, man.

19:27.440 --> 19:29.630
No big deal, I guess.

19:29.630 --> 19:34.220
What? It's a huge deal, Hori!
Look at the score!

19:38.190 --> 19:41.200
<b>East</b>

19:38.190 --> 19:41.200
<b>West</b>

19:43.630 --> 19:44.820
Come on, Remi.

19:45.210 --> 19:46.680
We need to put these chairs back.

19:46.680 --> 19:49.440
We were ahead until the afternoon.

19:50.110 --> 19:52.660
It's nice that Sengoku-kun 
won though, right?

19:55.410 --> 19:59.090
But you practiced so hard for the cheer.

20:04.010 --> 20:05.720
Not that hard.

20:06.320 --> 20:10.940
You were the cutest one out there.

20:10.940 --> 20:12.330
Sure, sure.

20:15.360 --> 20:19.110
<i>My nose got sunburned and it hurts.</i>

20:21.860 --> 20:24.570
<i>Shindo's gonna make fun of me.</i>

20:27.440 --> 20:29.370
Huh? Hori-san?

20:30.640 --> 20:31.370
Miyamura?

20:32.580 --> 20:35.940
Why are you in such a hurry?

20:36.860 --> 20:39.280
Wh-Why are you in a cheerleading outfit?

20:39.280 --> 20:40.830
Sports day is over!

20:40.830 --> 20:42.290
Oh, this?

20:42.290 --> 20:45.010
The girls are taking a group picture.

20:45.460 --> 20:47.620
I wore the boy's uniform 
for the competition,

20:47.620 --> 20:51.020
so I figured I could at least 
wear this for the group photo.

20:51.020 --> 20:53.440
You looked really good in that uniform.

20:53.440 --> 20:54.520
Really?

20:54.860 --> 20:58.310
I guess I'm the reason we won, then!

20:58.310 --> 21:00.570
<i>I'm so glad I got sunburned.</i>

21:04.980 --> 21:06.550
<i>The person who's been rooting for me</i>

21:06.940 --> 21:08.820
<i>since before sports day,</i>

21:09.350 --> 21:12.830
<i>even long before that,</i>

21:09.770 --> 21:11.010
Is your face red?

21:11.010 --> 21:12.000
I got sunburned.

21:14.210 --> 21:16.830
<i>is shining brighter than ever.</i>

21:17.210 --> 21:18.580
Am I cute?

21:18.580 --> 21:21.440
Kidding! Just imitating Ayasaki-san.

21:21.960 --> 21:23.110
You are cute.

21:24.050 --> 21:25.640
Super cute, in fact.

21:33.120 --> 21:34.350
Dummy!

21:34.350 --> 21:36.850
You big dummy!

21:42.000 --> 21:43.990
<i>Today might've been</i>

21:43.990 --> 21:45.320
Ow...

21:45.320 --> 21:50.240
<i>my first and last sports day...</i>

21:57.410 --> 21:59.290
It was fun.

22:04.280 --> 22:07.850
<i>That's how I felt after it was all over.</i>

23:36.560 --> 23:40.060
Next time
page.4 Hori Kotatsu
